|~ `::binding`, the kind of the record a declaration writes into its
   scope, and the laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSNAM#binding]. ~|

:binding
  |~~ A binding is the record a declaration writes: a name with its
      page, its value and where it came from, so what is named can be
      listed and asked like data. `env` answers the bindings a reader
      declared, and `binding` the record of a name,
      `::vec/count | binding | get /origin` answering `:qlang/vec`.

      It prints as a map under its tag, its fields read under the kind;
      the record of `:x 5` read from the cell `cell-1` is
      `::binding{:name :x :docs [] :value 5 :source ~(:x 5) :origin :cell-1}`.
      A binding no declaration wrote, a node a chain lays among them, holds
      no source.
      ::link~(::bind | doc) ::link~(::any/binding | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/names | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps |~~ The fields of the record, a map. ~~| ::map
    | reads :name |~~ The keyword the binding binds. ~~| /name ::keyword
    | reads :docs
        |~~ The docs of its page, one for each doc of the slot of its
            declaration.
        ~~|
        /docs [::doc]
    | reads :value |~~ What the name holds. ~~| /value
    | reads :source
        |~~ The quote of the step that declared it, null for a binding no
            declaration wrote.
        ~~|
        /source #[::null ::quote]
    | reads :origin
        |~~ The source or the cell it was read from, null for a name a call
            binds.
        ~~|
        /origin #[::keyword ::null]
    | proves :holdsTheValue
        |~~ The record of a name holds its value. ~~|
        ~(:x |~~ One. ~~| 1 | env | get /x | get /value | eq 1)
    | proves :holdsThePage
        |~~ The record of a name holds its page. ~~|
        ~(:x |~~ One. ~~| 1 | env | get /x | doc | content | eq "One.")
    | proves :holdsTheName
        |~~ The record of a name holds the name. ~~|
        ~(:x 1 | env | get /x | get /name | eq :x)
    | proves :holdsNoSourceForANodeAChainLays
        |~~ A binding no declaration wrote, a node a chain lays, holds no
            source.
        ~~|
        ~(::number/add/addend | binding | get /source | eq null)
    | proves :readsBackFromItsPrint
        |~~ The record of a name reads back from its print. ~~|
        ~(:x |~~ One. ~~| 5 | ::x | binding | :b it | print | parse | open | eq b)
    | proves :docs/NotGivenError/refusesARecordWithNoDocs
        |~~ A binding a reader writes holds every field of the record. ~~|
        ~(::binding{:name :x} !| tag | eq ::binding/docs/NotGivenError)
    | proves :name/KindNotTakenError/refusesANameThatIsNoKeyword
        |~~ The name of a binding is a keyword. ~~|
        ~(::binding{:name "x" :docs [] :value 1 :source null :origin null} !| tag | eq ::binding/name/KindNotTakenError)

